{
  "summary": "This review investigates rate capability limitations in lithium-rich manganese oxide (LRMO) cathodes, identifying three hierarchical kinetic bottlenecks: direct charge-transfer impediments, sluggish anionic redox kinetics, and degradation cascades. It demonstrates that the rate-determining step shifts from electron-transfer to ion-diffusion dominance, influenced by exchange and limiting current densities. The study emphasizes charging kinetics as more critical for fast charging than discharging and highlights methodological inconsistencies in cross-study C-rate comparisons that hinder performance evaluation. The findings provide a theoretical framework for designing high-rate LRMO cathodes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The rate-determining step shifts from electron-transfer to ion-diffusion dominance in LRMO cathodes",
    "Charging kinetics impose a more severe bottleneck for fast charging than discharging",
    "Methodological inconsistencies in C-rate comparisons due to electrode loading and testing variations limit cross-study performance evaluation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a hierarchical framework for understanding rate-limiting mechanisms in LRMO cathodes, enabling targeted design strategies to enhance high-rate performance for next-generation battery applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines the relationship between early-life farm exposure and food allergy, focusing on prenatal and childhood exposures. It synthesizes evidence that farm environments may promote immune tolerance through livestock contact, farm dust, microbial exposure, and diet. Protective effects are hypothesized to involve gut microbiome development, reduced inflammation, and regulatory T-cell responses. However, direct evidence for food allergy prevention remains limited compared to asthma, highlighting the need for mechanistic studies to identify actionable pathways for intervention.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Early farm exposures correlate with reduced food allergy risk through multiple environmental factors",
    "Protective mechanisms likely involve gut microbiome maturation and immune regulation",
    "Direct evidence linking farm exposure to clinically confirmed food allergy is limited compared to asthma"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review identifies critical pathways for understanding how early environmental exposures may prevent food allergy, emphasizing the need for mechanistic research to develop targeted interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils expressing Nlrp3 and Il1b, which drive pathogenic TH17 cell activation. After recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. The findings demonstrate that short-lived dietary states during specific temporal windows can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates acute type 17 skin inflammation to chronic obesity levels",
    "HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window blunts disease amplification",
    "Neutrophil-mediated NLRP3-IL-1β signaling licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, with persistent tissue-resident memory T cells causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that transient dietary states during narrow temporal windows can durably reprogram immune responses, revealing a mechanism by which short-lived physiological changes become embedded in tissue immune memory."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates converting industrial piezoelectric single-crystal debris into high-performance flexible 0-3 composites. Using ball-milling and dielectrophoresis-assisted curing, the researchers transformed PMN-PT debris into dispersible fillers that form vertically connected quasi-1-3 networks within a PDMS matrix. The resulting composite achieved a d33 of 118.5 pC N-1 while maintaining flexibility, demonstrating superior electromechanical properties for energy harvesting applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PMN-PT single-crystal debris was converted into high-performance flexible 0-3 piezoelectric composites via ball-milling and dielectrophoresis-assisted curing",
    "The composite achieved a d33 of 118.5 pC N-1 with retained mechanical flexibility",
    "Single-crystal debris exhibited stronger dielectrophoresis-induced enhancement than polycrystalline materials due to coherent electromechanical conversion"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable method for upcycling high-value piezoelectric single-crystal waste into flexible energy harvesters, advancing sustainable resource utilization in electromechanical systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed an ultrasound-triggered nanoplatform (MRPT) that integrates sonodynamic therapy (SDT) with immunotherapy. The platform generates reactive oxygen species under ultrasound, cleaves Diels-Alder bonds to release immunoadjuvant R837, and captures tumor-associated antigens via exposed maleimide groups. The system enhanced dendritic cell maturation, increased CD8+ T cell infiltration, and reduced regulatory T cells, achieving a 2.7-fold higher ovalbumin capture and a 40.6% rise in mature dendritic cells in the spleen.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ultrasound activation triggers ROS generation and Diels-Alder bond cleavage for R837 release",
    "Maleimide groups enable 2.7-fold higher ovalbumin capture compared to non-irradiated conditions",
    "The platform increased mature dendritic cells in spleen by 40.6% and reduced regulatory T cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that ultrasound-regulated antigen capture and immune stimulation can synergistically enhance sonodynamic immunotherapy efficacy through integrated tumor antigen presentation and immune activation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the limited neutron response in homogeneous lithium-aluminosilicate-glass scintillators by engineering fluoride-mediated host-activator interactions. The approach reconfigures the glass network to suppress electronic disorder and defect trapping while enabling higher cerium concentrations. Results show efficient neutron detection at 8003 photons per neutron, 6.8% energy resolution, and a neutron peak-to-trough ratio of 77:1. The material achieves single-digit neutron energy resolution and supports two-dimensional thermal-neutron imaging with 1.35 mm spatial resolution.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fluoride-mediated host-activator engineering suppresses electronic disorder and defect trapping in Ce3+-activated lithium aluminosilicate glasses",
    "The scintillator achieves 8003 photons per neutron with 6.8% energy resolution and 77:1 neutron peak-to-trough ratio",
    "Transparent plates exceeding 2 inches enable two-dimensional thermal-neutron imaging with 1.35 mm spatial resolution"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes homogeneous glass scintillators as viable platforms for high-performance thermal-neutron detection and imaging, achieving energy resolution comparable to crystalline scintillators and enabling scalable position-sensitive neutron imaging."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates sustainable soft electronic devices using recyclable elastomers and conductors. Researchers developed a multifunctional poly thioctic acid elastomer with high stretchability (435% strain), fracture energy (5.5 kJ/m²), adhesion energy on Cu (10.7 kJ/m²), and thermal conductivity (0.69 W/m·K). The system integrates recyclable elastic metallic conductors, enabling self-healing and full circuit restoration after mechanical rupture. The approach demonstrates a sustainable pathway for robust, recyclable soft electronics with broad applications in health monitoring and human-machine interfaces.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Poly thioctic acid elastomer achieves 435% strain stretchability and 5.5 kJ/m² fracture energy",
    "The elastomer exhibits 10.7 kJ/m² adhesion energy on copper and 0.69 W/m·K thermal conductivity",
    "Integrated recyclable conductors enable full circuit restoration after mechanical rupture through self-healing"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a recyclable soft electronic system with self-healing capabilities, advancing sustainable electronics design through material integration that maintains functionality after mechanical damage and supports circular manufacturing."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates ultralow-loading iridium-doped hollandite manganese oxide nanowires for acidic oxygen evolution reaction (OER) catalysis. The researchers developed a catalyst with 3 atomic percent iridium (<16 µgIr cm-2) integrated into a manganese dioxide framework. It reduced the overpotential at 10 mA cm-2 from 580 mV to 303 mV compared to undoped α-MnO2 and achieved Ir mass activity 10 times higher than commercial IrOx. The catalyst showed modest dissolution (79% Ir, 76% Mn retained after 6 h), with iridium remaining oxidized and bound to the framework while manganese underwent pH- and potential-dependent reduction and structural disorder. The findings emphasize the need to evaluate dissolution, reconstruction, and oxidation state together for designing efficient iridium-based catalysts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ultralow-loading iridium (3 at%, <16 µgIr cm-2) integrated into hollandite MnO2 framework",
    "Reduced OER overpotential from 580 mV to 303 mV at 10 mA cm-2 compared to undoped α-MnO2",
    "Modest dissolution (79% Ir, 76% Mn retained after 6 h) with iridium remaining oxidized and manganese undergoing pH- and potential-dependent reduction"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that ultralow iridium loading in hollandite manganese oxides can achieve high OER activity with minimal dissolution, providing critical insights for designing durable, iridium-efficient catalysts for acidic environments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates mixed-dimensional organic/inorganic heterostructures for high-performance short-wave infrared (SWIR) photodetection. By engineering a type-II band-aligned PTF/WSe2 heterostructure with optimized Schottky barriers, researchers achieved broadband photoresponsivity (103 A/W, 1060-1470 nm) and exceptional metrics at 1310 nm, including ultrahigh responsivity (2894 A/W) and robust detectivity (1.0×1012 Jones). The device demonstrated superior stability and performance over six months, highlighting its potential for next-generation SWIR detectors.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Optimized PTF/WSe2 heterostructure with 0.28 eV Schottky barrier achieves ultrahigh photoresponsivity (2894 A/W) at 1310 nm",
    "Broadband photoresponsivity of 103 A/W across 1060-1470 nm with 96% lower bias voltage versus standalone PTF",
    "Exceptional long-term stability with maintained performance after six months of ambient storage"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes mixed-dimensional heterostructures as a viable pathway to high-performance, stable SWIR photodetectors through synergistic design principles, addressing critical challenges in carrier collection and interface engineering."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a dual-locked NIR-II nanoagent responsive to H2S and NO for colon cancer theranostics. The nanoagent, CTBNN-NPs, remains inactive until colon cancer cells internalize it, where H2S and in situ released NO activate tandemly, enabling NIR-II fluorescence imaging at 1200 nm. It also shows enhanced photothermal and photodynamic effects, achieving cancer cell elimination through combined imaging-guided phototherapy and NO therapy, with limited efficacy in other cancer models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CTBNN-NPs are activated by H2S and in situ NO release in colon cancer cells",
    "The nanoagent enables NIR-II fluorescence imaging at 1200 nm for colon cancer detection",
    "It achieves efficient colon cancer elimination via photothermal and NO gas therapy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a novel dual-locked nanoagent design that integrates gas-responsive activation with NIR-II imaging for targeted cancer theranostics, advancing strategies for precise tumor treatment."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates controlling polymorph formation in non-fullerene acceptors for organic solar cells. Using a carbon disulfide and o-xylene mixed solvent system, researchers selectively induced a specific polymorph (Form II) of BTP-eC9. Form II demonstrated enhanced optoelectronic properties, including longer exciton diffusion length, balanced charge mobility, and reduced recombination. Devices based on Form II achieved 20.61% power conversion efficiency, a 27.0% improvement over Form I devices (16.23%), with scalable production via slot-die coating.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Form II of BTP-eC9 exhibits extended exciton diffusion length and balanced charge mobility compared to Form I",
    "Form II-based devices achieve 20.61% power conversion efficiency, a 27.0% relative improvement over Form I devices",
    "Slot-die coating enables scalable fabrication of flexible organic solar cells with 17.93% efficiency"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a practical method for solution-processed polymorph control in organic solar cells, linking molecular packing to device performance through selective crystallization strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed pH-responsive synthetic cells that convert external acidity into nucleic acid signals to drive in situ protein synthesis. The system uses gramicidin A channels for pH sensing, triplex-formin ssDNA for acid-triggered release, and toehold switch RNA for translation activation. Tuning ssDNA annealing lengths controls the trigger-release pH, enabling programmable protein synthesis in alginate hydrogels. Cell-penetrating peptides allow selective protein release and target binding, demonstrating environmental acidity sensing for on-demand biomolecule production.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The synthetic cells convert external pH changes into nucleic acid information for in situ protein synthesis",
    "Tuning ssDNA annealing lengths controls the trigger-release pH threshold",
    "The system retains functionality in alginate hydrogels with cell-penetrating peptides enabling selective protein release"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a molecular transduction strategy for programming synthetic cell materials to sense environmentally relevant acidity and generate functional biomolecules on demand."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a thermochemically active hydrogel designed to suppress thermal runaway propagation in lithium-ion batteries. Using boric acid as a cross-linker in poly(AMPS) hydro, the hydrogel enhances mechanical strength by 567% and provides dual-mode protection: synergistic heat absorption via water evaporation and boric acid dehydration, and in situ formation of a ceramic-carbon hybrid barrier. At 25 wt% boric acid, the hydrogel reduces adjacent cell peak temperatures by over 500°C, demonstrating significant thermal runaway suppression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Boric acid cross-linking in poly(AMPS) hydrogel increases compressive strength by 567%",
    "The composite exhibits volumetric enthalpy >2000 J cm-3 through water evaporation and boric acid dehydration",
    "At 25 wt% boric acid, the hydrogel forms a ceramic-carbon hybrid barrier reducing adjacent cell peak temperatures by >500°C"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a general design principle for battery safety materials through reactive fillers that enable multi-stage energy management and tailored barrier synthesis, advancing thermal runaway suppression strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of high-fidelity multi-modal temperature-humidity sensing without cross-talk by developing a Pd single-atom engineered Janus BiOCl/MXene heterostructure. The material achieves segregated electronic and ionic pathways: humidity triggers ultra-fast proton conduction via localized potential wells and Pd sites, while temperature induces entropy-driven carrier diffusion. The sensor demonstrates rapid response/recovery (37.5/50 ms humidity; 25/62.5 ms temperature) and robust durability, enabling closed-loop wound healing monitoring with machine learning.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Humidity fluctuations induce ultra-fast proton conduction through localized potential wells and Pd sites",
    "Temperature gradients cause entropy-driven carrier diffusion in the conductive MXene network",
    "The sensor exhibits rapid response/recovery times (37.5/50 ms humidity; 25/62.5 ms temperature) and 5000-cycle durability"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a fundamental mechanism for self-decoupled multi-modal sensing through electron-ion synergistic pathways, advancing flexible electronics for real-time physiological monitoring without post-processing."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a defined matrix system for human intestinal organoids (hIOs) by replacing Matrigel with recombinant human substrates and PEG hydrogels. Transcriptomic analysis revealed epithelial cells in both matrices closely resemble duodenal reference populations, with fetal-like expression patterns. PEG culture induced subtle shifts in epithelial differentiation and mesenchymal ECM-remodelling pathways. Matrix stiffness increased MUC2-positive cells in epithelia but had minimal effects on mesenchymal responses. The platform enables controlled investigation of matrix cues in intestinal development and fibrosis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Epithelial cells in both matrices show high transcriptional similarity to fetal duodenal reference populations",
    "PEG culture induces subtle shifts in epithelial differentiation-associated gene expression and mesenchymal ECM-remodelling pathways",
    "Increasing matrix stiffness increases MUC2-positive cells in epithelia but has minimal effects on mesenchymal responses"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a defined platform for studying matrix-dependent epithelial and mesenchymal responses in intestinal organoids, enabling precise manipulation of physical cues to investigate developmental and fibrotic mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the limitation of NIR-responsive polymer actuators by developing skunk cabbage-inspired aggregation-induced emission (AIE) luminogen-doped polyimides. The approach integrates ultra-low concentrations (0.25 wt%) of AIEgens into Janus-structured polymers to achieve 980 nm photothermal absorption, enhanced mechanical properties (>100 MPa), and multicolor fluorescence. Actuators demonstrate ultrafast bending (900°/s) under NIR light, enabling programmable motions via multiwavelength responses. The findings advance smart materials for precise 980 nm actuation without compromising mechanical integrity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Integration of AIEgens at 0.25 wt% into Janus polyimides enables 980 nm photothermal absorption",
    "Actuators achieve ultrafast bending (900°/s) and multicolor fluorescence under NIR illumination",
    "Materials maintain mechanical strength (>100 MPa) while supporting programmable multiwavelength actuation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a strategy for NIR-responsive actuators that overcome wavelength limitations and maintain mechanical robustness, enabling precise 980 nm actuation with multicolor functionality for advanced smart materials applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates composition-structure-property relationships in quaternary perovskitoids using megalibraries. Researchers synthesized one million positionally encoded Cs3Sb2-xBixBr9-yIy microcrystals via parylene templates on 2 cm² chips. Micro-area x-ray diffraction and spectroscopy revealed a non-monotonic bandgap shift with Br content, minimizing at 33% Br due to halide-segregated heterostructures. Sb-rich compositions stabilized these heterostructures, enabling rapid evaluation of optoeaspects like bandgap and phase purity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A non-monotonic bandgap shift occurs with increasing Br content, reaching minimum at 33% Br",
    "Halide-segregated heterostructures form I-rich shells around Br-rich layered cores",
    "Sb-rich compositions stabilize heterostructure formation, enhancing phase separation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a megalibrary approach for rapidly mapping complex composition-structure-property relationships in perovskitoids, advancing materials discovery through high-throughput characterization of optoelectronic properties."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates stretchable fully π-conjugated polymer films for flexible light-emitting diodes. The researchers developed supramolecular micro-crosslinked networks using oxime-urethane and hydrogen bonds to prevent irreversible chain slippage. Films achieved >40% elongation at break and maintained stable green emission in flexible PLEDs with brightness up to 3300 cd cm-2. The devices demonstrated cycle-deformation stability without significant performance degradation under tensile strains exceeding 20%.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Supramolecular micro-crosslinked networks prevent irreversible chain slippage in stretchable polymer films",
    "Films achieved >40% elongation at break while maintaining stable green emission in PLEDs",
    "Flexible devices retained performance under cyclic deformation with tensile strains >20%"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a supramolecular strategy to achieve highly stretchable, recoverable polymer films with enhanced mechanical stability for durable flexible optoelectronic applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates polymer-directed synthesis of mesoporous single-crystalline Mn2OBO3 for lithium-ion battery anodes. Using polyethyleneimine (PEI) as a bifunctional regulator, the researchers modulate hydrolysis and condensation to form a hybrid precursor, followed by hydrothermal treatment and calcination. The resulting material achieves a reversible capacity of 1440 mAh g-1 at 0.2 A g-1, significantly exceeding bulk Mn2OBO3. The approach demonstrates template-free synthesis of porous single-crystalline borates with potential for doping and energy storage applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Polyethyleneimine (PEI) coordinates Mn2+ ions and hydrogen bonds with borate ions to regulate hydrolysis and condensation",
    "Single-crystalline Mn2OBO3 nanobelts yield a reversible capacity of 1440 mAh g-1 at 0.2 A g-1",
    "The polymer-directed strategy enables template-free synthesis and is extendable to doped Mn2OBO3 for energy storage"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a polymer-directed method for template-free synthesis of mesoporous single-crystalline borates, advancing porous material design for high-capacity lithium-ion battery anodes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated efficient inhaled nucleic acid delivery to the lung using a novel thio-amino polymer (P81). The researchers evaluated P81's transfection potency via nebulized mRNA, assessing cell-type specificity through single-cell spatial transcriptomics. Results showed P81 achieved 34.1- to 77.8-fold higher transfection efficiency than prior polymers, delivered to bronchial epithelial cells, tracheal stem cells, and 54% of distal lung cells, and suppressed SARS-CoV-2 infection without significant toxicity in rodents.",
  "key_findings": [
    "P81 demonstrated 34.1- to 77.8-fold higher transfection efficiency than previous polymers for nebulized mRNA delivery",
    "Spatial transcriptomics revealed P81 delivered to bronchial airway epithelial cells, tracheal basal stem cells, and 54% of distal lung cells",
    "P81 enabled SARS-CoV-2 suppression and showed low toxicity in rodent nebulization studies"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a highly efficient, safe, and broadly applicable polymer-based delivery system for inhaled nucleic acids, advancing therapeutic potential for respiratory diseases through improved transfection and targeted delivery."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates in situ topological dealloying to create atomically coupled metal-oxide heterostructures with enhanced interface properties. The approach involves synthesizing perovskite, spinel, columbite, and vanadate oxides via this method, enabling high-density magnetic nanoalloys within dielectric matrices. Results show coexisting interfacial charge polarization and vortex-like spin textures, along with broadband GHz-frequency absorption (up to .6 GHz) and rapid electromagnetic-to-thermal energy conversion under microwaves.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Atomically interconnected metal-oxide interfaces via in situ topological dealloying",
    "Coexistence of interfacial charge polarization and vortex-like spin textures",
    "Broadband GHz-frequency absorption (up to 6.6 GHz) and rapid electromagnetic-to-thermal energy conversion"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a general synthetic strategy for engineering metal-oxide heterostructures with strong charge-spin interactions, advancing functional materials design for energy conversion and electronic applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates transforming conventional cement into passive cooling materials by structurally programming cement hydration. The approach involves hydrogel-confined mineralization to create a hierarchically porous calcium-silicate-hydrate network with broadband light scattering, vapor transport, and thermal insulation. The material achieves ∼95% solar reflectance and ∼9.8% infrared emissivity, enabling evaporative cooling under humid conditions. Life-cycle analysis suggests this strategy reduces cement's carbon footprint by integrating daytime radiative cooling into building envelopes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The hydrogel-confined mineralization process generates a hierarchically porous calcium-silicate-hydrate network",
    "The material achieves ∼95% solar reflectance and ∼98% infrared emissivity without photonic fillers",
    "The network enables sustained evaporative cooling under humid or cloudy conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a scalable method to convert high-emission cement into carbon-mitigating building materials through passive daytime radiative cooling, addressing a critical challenge in sustainable construction."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates optimizing quasi-solid-state polymer electrolytes for lithium metal batteries by tuning monomer structures with varying Li+ affinity. The research demonstrates that weakly coordinating segments, like fluorinated ethers, reduce cation-transport friction by minimizing Li+ coupling, leading to high ionic conductivity and stable performance. The electrolyte enables long cycle life (>520 cycles), wide temperature operation (-5.0°C to +90°C), and high energy density (550 Wh kg-1) in practical cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Weakly coordinating segments (e.g., fluorinated ethers) minimize Li+ coupling, enhancing cation transport pathways",
    "Crosslinked polymer electrolytes achieve high ionic conductivity and stable operation across -50°C to +90°C",
    "Industrial Li metal pouch cells maintain >520 cycles and 550 Wh kg-1 energy density at low electrolyte dosage (1.3 g Ah-1)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a design principle for low-friction ion transport in crosslinked polymer electrolytes, advancing fundamental understanding of segmental solvation effects critical for high-performance lithium metal batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated a biomimetic hydrogel strategy for articular cartilage repair using coaxial bioprinting to create a sheath-core structure. The approach integrated a poly(ethylene glycol)-alginate sheath for mechanical support and immunoprotection with a chondrogenic core gelatin methacryloyl-alginate-decellularized extracellular matrix. The design enabled stem cell survival >89% under pro-inflammatory conditions and promoted cartilage regeneration in rabbit models, achieving defect filling and glycosaminoglycan-rich tissue. The findings demonstrate a functional biomaterial platform addressing joint inflammation challenges.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The poly(ethylene glycol)-alginate sheath provided size-selective diffusion barrier activity, blocking inflammatory cytokines (>40 kDa) while allowing nutrient and oxygen permeation",
    "Stem cell viability remained >89% under pro-inflammatory conditions within the hydrogel construct",
    "The biomaterial achieved defect filling and regeneration of glycosaminoglycan-rich hyaline-like cartilage in rabbit osteochondral defects"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This biomimetic hydrogel design integrates mechanical support, immunoprotection, and chondrogenic differentiation capabilities to overcome inflammatory barriers in articular cartilage repair."
}
